.snakemake/

config/config_custom.yaml

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# MkDocs build output. The Markdown sources in docs/ and mkdocs.yml ARE tracked;
# site/ is the generated HTML, rebuilt on demand and published to the gh-pages
# branch rather than committed here.
site/

# ISEScan scratch files, which land in the working directory rather than in the
# output directory. ISEScan needs a "file of filenames" to feed its own predictor,
# so it writes a one-line file holding the path to the assembly, uses it, and
# deletes it again. Two details make it land here: it opens that file with a
# relative path, so it goes to wherever Snakemake was launched from (this
# directory), and it builds the name from the assembly's parent folder — which in
# BacFlux is the sample — giving {sample}_contigs_final.fasta.list.
#
# It cleans up after itself, so you normally never see one. You will see them while
# a run with the mobilome module is in progress, and they survive if ISEScan is
# interrupted. Ignoring them keeps sample names out of the repository.
*_contigs_final.fasta.list

# Scratch output from running a mobilome script by hand. The naming and
# colocalisation scripts take --out-* paths, so testing one from the repository
# root leaves its tables there; three of them were committed by accident once.
# The real fixtures live in workflow/scripts/80_mobilome/testdata/ and are named
# *_synthetic.tsv, which these patterns deliberately do not match.
/synth.tsv
/synth_*.tsv
